# Martin & Moyce (1952) collapse of liquid column -- surge-front position (as shipped by Lethe CFD)
# Original reference (as cited by Lethe): J.C. Martin et al., "Part IV. An experimental study of the collapse
#   of liquid columns on a rigid horizontal plane", Philos. Trans. R. Soc. Lond. Ser. Math. Phys. Sci.
#   244 (882), 312-324, Mar. 1952, doi:10.1098/rsta.1952.0006
# Secondary source (arrays copied verbatim):
#   Lethe, examples/multiphysics/dam-break/dam-break-2d.py
#   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chaos-polymtl/lethe/master/examples/multiphysics/dam-break/dam-break-2d.py
#   https://github.com/chaos-polymtl/lethe/blob/master/examples/multiphysics/dam-break/dam-break-2d.py?plain=1
#   Code: "#Experimental data from Martin & Moyce 1952 [1]"
#         x_exp = [...]  (plotted on x-axis labelled tau), y_exp = [...] (plotted on y-axis labelled delta)
# Nondimensionalisation used by Lethe for its simulation curve (same axes):
#   tau   = t*sqrt(2*g/L1)  (L1 = initial column width; Lethe case: width 3.5, height 7 -> n^2 = 2)
#   delta = x/L1            (x = surge-front position)
#   NOTE: Lethe adds time_correction = 0.175 to its SIMULATION times (not to x_exp); experimental values unmodified.
# Which a (1.125 in or 2.25 in) and whether digitised or tabulated is NOT stated by Lethe.
# Rows: 14
# tau     delta
